# Zapp sibling repository dependency lockfile.
# CI verifies that the checked-out zappMessaging SHA matches before building.
# Update when intentionally bumping a sibling dependency.

# The published SDK, whose history is squashed and so carries its own commit ids:
# this repository pins the mirror, not the development repo it is published from.
# GitHub: https://github.com/JustZappIt/zappmessaging-sdk
zappMessaging=a8b88ed4f6cc22382a4c79167340031aa12c42b1

# bare-kit is a direct clone of holepunchto/bare-kit v2.0.0 with no Zapp modifications.
# GitHub: https://github.com/holepunchto/bare-kit
# The local ../bare-kit/ directory has no git history; CI checks out the pinned commit.
# Update both this SHA and the workflow ref when upgrading bare-kit.
bare-kit=15a3569f3d704de7151761051c8d9cc2e299414f

# zcash-android-wallet-sdk is resolved from Maven snapshots, not includeBuild: upstream
# zodl ships SDK_INCLUDED_BUILD_PATH blank, but it does not leave the SDK floating: on
# maint/v3.10.x it sets SDK_COMMIT_PIN, and its CI builds the SDK from that exact commit
# rather than resolving the published artifact. We now match that, both the version and the
# pin, so our CI compiles the same SDK tree upstream's does. The SHA below is that pin, and
# unlike before it IS a build input in CI (.github/actions/setup-sdk-companion reads
# SDK_COMMIT_PIN from gradle.properties); locally, an unset SDK_INCLUDED_BUILD_PATH still
# resolves the Maven snapshot.
#
# ON v3.1.0, for coinholder polling: the first SDK line with the public VotingSdk facade and a
# native library built with cfg(zcash_voting) (63 voting JNI symbols; 3.0.1 exports none).
#
# Slipstream is NOT lost by this bump. At 3.1.0 the AGPL engine was split out of the
# MIT-published zcash-android-sdk into its own zcash-android-sdk-slipstream artifact, which still
# arrives transitively via sdk-incubator and is what the wallet runs (verified on-device).
# WalletCoordinator's isSlipstreamEnabled parameter is gone only because the engine stopped being
# opt-in per wallet.
#
# The pin is what keeps that true. -SNAPSHOT is mutable: SDK commit 6b4d6339 ("MOB-1757: Remove
# the Slipstream sync engine and its AGPL dependency") deletes it outright and adds a cargo-deny
# licence gate, so a republish of 3.1.0-SNAPSHOT could have dropped Slipstream with no code change
# and no build failure. 6b4d6339 is NOT an ancestor of the pin below (verified: 62 slipstream
# paths still present in that tree), so pinning freezes Slipstream in place instead of leaving it
# to the next publish. Re-check that ancestry whenever this pin moves. See docs/voting.md.
#
# GitHub: https://github.com/zcash/zcash-android-wallet-sdk
zcashAndroidWalletSdk=0ef67b411f0a51aae00346fef18286505e1bcfd1
